   229	
   230	    Input structure:
   231	    - The grid is always 11x11 with a fixed green 3x3 target around one red center, orange floor, optional magenta walls, and maroon pixels scattered on floor cells.
   232	    - Some maroons are flood-fill reachable from the target through floor/maroon corridors; others may be sealed off behind walls as distractors.
   233	
   234	    Rule:
   235	    - Flood-fill outward from passable cells adjacent to the target, traversing only floor or maroon cells, and keep only reachable maroons as candidates.
   236	    - Rank candidates primarily by row position; within the same row, prefer smaller flood-fill distance to the target; if a row still has multiple candidates at the same distance, use smaller column first.
   237	    - Move up to nine ranked maroons into the destination in destination row-major order, and clear their source cells back to floor.
   238	
   239	    Key insight:
   240	    - Walls still determine eligibility, but the movement order is no longer purely distance-based and no longer purely scan-order either; you must combine visible row position with local corridor distance inside each row.
